[15:08:08Z] SHELL:    which <word>  (verb? program? neither), history [n] [-c], sleep <ms>
[15:08:08Z]           env  (build facts + shell variables), set [NAME [VALUE]] | set -u NAME
[15:08:08Z]           (no $VAR expansion yet - the store is readable by `env`; expansion is midden M2)
[15:08:08Z] STORAGE:  df | mount  (volumes: capacity, used, free, mount point, posture)
[15:08:08Z]           fdisk -l  (block devices: vendor, block size, blocks, capacity)
[15:08:08Z]           dd if=<lba> | dd of=<lba> byte=<0xNN>  (ONE raw 512-byte block; no file is involved)
[15:08:08Z] FILES:    ls [-l] [dir], cd [dir], pwd, cat <path>
[15:08:08Z] PAGING:   head <path> [n], tail <path> [n]  (first / last n lines, default 10)
[15:08:08Z] TEXT:     grep [-i] [-n] [-v] [-c] <pattern> <path>  (fixed string; ^ and $ anchor)
[15:08:08Z]           wc [-l|-w|-c] <path>  (lines, words, bytes)
[15:08:08Z] WRITE:    touch <path>, write <path> <text>, append <path> <text>, rm [-r] [-f] <path>
[15:08:08Z] DIRS:     mkdir <path>, rmdir <path>  (create / remove empty directories)
[15:08:08Z] MOUNT:    mount write|append|rm|mkdir <path> [text]  (the one namespace, by prefix)
[15:08:08Z]           rm -r <dir>  (recursively delete a directory tree; root refused)
[15:08:08Z] COPY:     cp [-f] <src> <dst>  (copy a file; cp FILE DIR/ lands as DIR/<leaf>)
[15:08:08Z]           cp -r <srcdir> <dst>  (recursively copy a directory tree)
[15:08:08Z] MOVE:     mv [-f] <src...> <dst>  (move/rename a file or dir, O(1); mv SRC DIR/ lands as DIR/<leaf>)
[15:08:08Z] FLAGS:    default is no-clobber; -f = force overwrite (rm: quiet on missing), -n = no-clobber
[15:08:08Z] WILDCARD: * / ? in the last path component - ls/cat/rm/cp/mv expand it (e.g. rm *.TMP, cp *.TXT DOCS/)
[15:08:08Z]           (create/edit/delete/copy/move files & dirs anywhere in the tree; sync = write-through, durable)
[15:08:08Z] TREE:     find [root] <pattern>  (recursive glob search), du [dir]  (recursive size tally)
[15:08:08Z]           uptime  (seconds since boot; shows the wall clock when set)
[15:08:08Z] INSPECT:  stat <path>  (full on-disk detail), hexdump <path> [off] [len]  (bounded)
[15:08:08Z] NATIVE:   the plain file verbs reach the native volume: `/` native, /boot the boot FAT, /usb stick
[15:08:08Z]           setfattr <path> <key>=<value>, setfattr -x <key> <path>  (typed attributes: 42 1.5 "s" b64:.. [f,f])
[15:08:08Z]           getfattr <path> [key]  (one or all attributes), query <expr>  (id path of every match)
[15:08:08Z] SNAP:     snap list, snap create <name>, snap drop <gen>  (retained roots / snapshots)
[15:08:08Z]           snap ls <gen> [path], snap cat <gen> <path>  (read a snapshot; current-ACL enforced)
[15:08:08Z] CLOCK:    date, date -s YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]  (seeds mtime stamps; unset = honest dashes)
[15:08:08Z]           time  (shared civil clock: ISO-8601 UTC + source; unsynced until SNTP/date -s)
[15:08:08Z] SMP:      ps (per-CPU run queues)
[15:08:08Z]           <name>      (just type it: lumen opens its window and the prompt returns; net runs, then prints its exit)
[15:08:08Z]           the .elf is optional (lumen finds LUMEN.ELF); the program says how it runs: a window or a server detaches, else foreground
[15:08:08Z] POWER:    reboot (warm reboot), shutdown|off (power off, cold-boot-ready) - via the platform firmware
[15:08:08Z] NETWORK:  ifconfig  (NIC: MAC, link, counters), ping <ip> [count], arp <ip>
[15:08:08Z]           nc [-u] <ip> <port> [message]  (TCP connect+exchange; -u = one UDP datagram)
[15:08:08Z]           curl [http://]<ip>[:port][/path]  (HTTP/1.0 GET, printed)
[15:08:08Z] BENCH:    tste (in-OS self-test suite), panic (enter the exception path deliberately)
[15:08:08Z]           run <path>  (load + run an ELF64 in the foreground)
[15:08:08Z]           screenshot  (panel -> SCREEN<n>.PNG at the volume root; n = first free 0-99)
